# CUSV ArduRover skid-steer output mapping (found missing, 2026-08-09, while
# investigating a reported "vehicle deviating from the goal / speed too
# slow" symptom).
#
# CUSV has twin differential thrusters (model.sdf's motor_port_joint /
# motor_stbd_joint, control channels 0/2 -> SERVO1/SERVO3), but without
# this file CUSV boots with ArduRover's plain factory defaults --
# SERVO1_FUNCTION=26 (GroundSteering, for a car-style rudder) and
# SERVO3_FUNCTION=70 (plain Throttle) -- neither of which is the
# skid-steer mixing ArduRover actually needs to turn a twin-thruster hull.
# Confirmed live: with the factory defaults, SERVO_OUTPUT_RAW's servo1 and
# servo3 stayed pinned identically (e.g. both 1900) regardless of a
# growing cross-track error -- the boat drove in a straight line and
# never turned toward its waypoint at all, independent of and in addition
# to a separate thrust-direction bug in model.sdf (also fixed the same
# session). SERVO_FUNCTION 73/74 (ThrottleLeft/ThrottleRight) are
# ArduRover's own skid-steer functions -- they make the motor library
# mix steering + throttle into differential left/right output internally,
# instead of expecting a single combined throttle plus a separate
# steering-servo signal. This is the same fix
# vehicle_twins/mass_resilient_cusv/hardened.parm needs (and gets,
# separately, since ardu_defaults files aren't merged -- SITL only
# accepts one).
SERVO1_FUNCTION 73
SERVO3_FUNCTION 74
